{"id": "section-body-00915", "title": "Cardiac Tamponade", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-00915", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Cardiac Tamponade", "runs": [{"text": "Cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Tamponade"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1890"}}, {"id": "body-00916", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cardiac tamponade is the result of compression of the myocardium by fluid, gas, pus, blood, or a combination of substances. It occurs in a physiological continuum reflecting the amount of fluid, the rate of accumulation, and the nature of the heart.", "runs": [{"text": "Cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tamponade"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "result"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "compression"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "myocardium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fluid,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gas,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "combination"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "substances. It occurs in a physiological continuum reflecting the amount of fluid, the rate of accumulation, and the nature of the heart."}]}, {"id": "body-00917", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The result is increased pericardial pressure, which causes decreased ventricle compliance and decreased flow of blood into the right ventricle, which eventually leads to decreased cardiac output. Conditions that may predispose a patient to pericardial effusion and tamponade include trauma, radiation exposure, Tb pericarditis, renal failure (uremic pericarditis), autoimmune diseases, drugs that induce a lupus-like syndrome, hypothyroidism, or ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome.", "runs": [{"text": "The result is increased pericardial pressure, which causes decreased ventricle compliance and decreased flow of blood into the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "right"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ventricle,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eventually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leads"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "decreased"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "output."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Conditions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "predispose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pericardial effusion and tamponade include trauma, radiation exposure, Tb pericarditis, renal failure (uremic pericarditis), autoimmune diseases, drugs that induce a lupus-like syndrome, hypothyroidism, or ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome."}]}, {"id": "body-00918", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentations", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00919", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Chest pain and dyspnea", "runs": [{"text": "Chest"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dyspnea"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00920", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pulsus paradoxus >10 mm Hg", "runs": [{"text": "Pulsus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "paradoxus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">10"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mm"}, {"text": " Hg"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00921", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Beck’s triad includes low blood pressure, elevated jugular venous distention, and decreased heart sounds.", "runs": [{"text": "Beck’s triad includes low blood pressure, elevated jugular venous distention, and decreased heart "}, {"text": "sounds."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00922", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "In the absence of hypotension and tension pneumothorax in a patient with PEA, consider the diagnosis of cardiac tamponade.", "runs": [{"text": "In"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "absence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hypotension"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tension"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pneumothorax"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PEA,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "consider"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosis of cardiac tamponade."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00924", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00925", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Bedside ultrasound and ECHO, POC, ECG, Blood gases, Serum Electrolytes, Troponins, Pericardial fluid analysis- biochemistry, microbiology and cytology, Serum creatinine and urea, and/or Chest X-ray", "runs": [{"text": "Bedside"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ultrasound"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ECHO,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "POC,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ECG,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gases,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Serum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Electrolytes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Troponins,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pericardial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fluid analysis- biochemistry, microbiology and cytology, Serum creatinine and urea, and/or Chest X-ray"}]}, {"id": "body-00927", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non- Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00928", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Perform both primary and secondary assessments and provide appropriate interventions.", "runs": [{"text": "Perform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assessments"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "provide"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "appropriate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "interventions."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00929", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Give oxygen if hypoxic or increased work of breathing", "runs": [{"text": "Give"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oxygen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hypoxic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increased"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "work"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "breathing"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00930", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Connect the patient to a cardiac monitor and obtain vital signs", "runs": [{"text": "Connect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monitor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "obtain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00931", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pericardiocentesis is the definitive management", "runs": [{"text": "Pericardiocentesis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "definitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1872"}}, {"id": "body-00933", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00934", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: sodium chloride 0.9% (IV): Adults 1-2 litres; Pediatrics 20ml/kg to increase right-sided filling pressure", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "sodium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chloride"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.9%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV):"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adults"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1-2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "litres;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pediatrics"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20ml/kg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increase"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "right-sided"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "filling"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pressure"}]}, {"id": "body-00935-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note", "runs": [{"text": "Note", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-00935-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The definitive treatment for cardiac tamponade is pericardiocentesis. A cardiology consultation or referral is strongly recommended. In emergency settings, pericardiocentesis may be performed by a qualified and experienced medical practitioner in the emergency department.", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "definitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tamponade"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pericardiocentesis."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiology"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "consultation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "referral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "strongly recommended. In emergency settings, pericardiocentesis may be performed by a qualified and experienced medical practitioner in the emergency department."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1883"}}, {"id": "body-00935-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "All patients with cardiac tamponade require inpatient management in an intensive care unit setting/HDU.", "runs": [{"text": "All"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tamponade"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "require"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inpatient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "intensive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "care"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unit"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "setting/HDU."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1883"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Approach to patients with emergency conditions", "start": "body-00915", "end": "body-00935-textbox1-00003"}}